<title>SWEDEN: Trading in Skandia, Stadshypotek suspended-bourse.</title>
<headline>Trading in Skandia, Stadshypotek suspended-bourse.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stockholm bourse said on Monday that it had suspended trading in insurer Skandia and mortgage bank Stadshypotek following a merger announcement earlier in the morning.</p>
<p>The two companies announced a merger to form a new company, Skandia Stadsshypotek, with total assets of about 500 billion crowns, the largest insurance group in the Nordic region.</p>
<p>The two companies have called a press conference at 0930 GMT.</p>
<p>Skandia was last traded at 208.5 crowns and Stadshypotek at 198 crowns.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1045</p>
